<item>
            <title>[MAHOUT-1960] Flipped sign in the SparseSparseDrmTimer.mscala causes Desnse Matrix multiplication</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MAHOUT-1960</link>
                <project id="12310751" key="MAHOUT">Mahout</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;tt&gt;SparseSparseDrmTimer.mscala&lt;/tt&gt; with the signature: &lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt; def timeSparseDRMMMul(m: Int, n: Int, s: Int, para: Int, pctDense: Double = .20, seed: Long = 1234L): Long = {&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;the &lt;tt&gt;pctDense&lt;/tt&gt; argument indicates the percent of nonZero elements in the matrix. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As is the code to produce a random DRM for testing is as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;  val drmA = drmParallelizeEmpty(m , s, para).mapBlock(){
       &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;case&lt;/span&gt; (keys,block:Matrix) =&amp;gt;
         val R =  scala.util.Random
         R.setSeed(seed)
         val blockB = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; SparseRowMatrix(block.nrow, block.ncol) 
         blockB := {x =&amp;gt; &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; (R.nextDouble &amp;gt; pctDense) R.nextDouble &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; x }
       (keys -&amp;gt; blockB)
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The greater than sign in line:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    blockB := &lt;/p&gt;
{x =&amp;gt; if (R.nextDouble &amp;gt; pctDense) R.nextDouble else x }
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;should be a less than sign; i.e.:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;     blockB := &lt;/p&gt;
{x =&amp;gt; if (R.nextDouble &amp;lt; pctDense) R.nextDouble else x }
&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This incorrect sign produces matrices of Incorrect density and can cause OOM errors.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
